// org.openqa.selenium.io — pure-leaf Java module (no internal deps).
//
// Seven Java sources (CircularOutputStream, FileHandler,
// MultiOutputStream, Read, TemporaryFilesystem, Zip, package-info),
// one external Maven dep (`org.jspecify:jspecify` for the
// `@NullMarked` package annotation), no `//java/...` internal
// sibling deps. Selected as the second demonstration leaf (after
// `status/`) because it's the smallest tractable target that
// **consumes the shared BOM file** rather than inlining the version.
//
// Upstream Bazel equivalent (java/src/org/openqa/selenium/io/BUILD.bazel):
//
//     java_library(
//         name = "io",
//         srcs = glob(["*.java"]),
//         deps = [artifact("org.jspecify:jspecify")],
//     )
//
// aeb translation:
//
//   - `srcs = glob(["*.java"])` → `java.javac(b)` default mode
//     picks up `*.java` in source_dir.
//   - `artifact("org.jspecify:jspecify")` — the Bazel form is
//     unversioned because rules_jvm_external looks the version up
//     in `maven_install.json`. The aeb form loads the shared
//     `../../../../selenium-deps.bom.ae` (which pins jspecify to
//     1.0.0) and declares the coord unversioned via
//     `dep(b, "org.jspecify:jspecify")` — the BOM supplies the
//     pinned version to aeb-resolve.jar.
//
// This pattern is the load-bearing one for scaling Java conversion:
// shared `.bom.ae` carries the closure pin set; each leaf declares
// its direct coords with version inline (so each dep edge is
// greppable from this file alone). The unbridged alternative (parse
// `maven_install.json`) would have moved rules_jvm_external's data
// model into aeb; see Aeb_vs_Bazel.md.
//
// Relative path note: this leaf sits at
// `java/src/org/openqa/selenium/io/`, five directories below
// `java/`, so `../../../../../selenium-deps.bom.ae`.

import build
import build (dep)
import maven (load_bom_file)
import java
import java (release)

main() {
    b = build.start()
    load_bom_file(b, "../../../../../selenium-deps.bom.ae")
    dep(b, "org.jspecify:jspecify:1.0.0")
    java.javac(b) {
        release("17")
    }
}
